config DEBUG_DEV
	bool "Devices which can show debug output"
	depends on DM
	help
	  Enable a uclass for devices which can get a message out of U-Boot
	  without using the console. These are called explicitly from code
	  being debugged, rather than being wired up as a console, so they
	  work even when the console is unavailable or is itself the thing
	  under investigation.

if DEBUG_DEV

config DEBUG_EM100
	bool "Debug output through a Dediprog EM100Pro"
	depends on DM_SPI
	help
	  Send debug output to a Dediprog EM100Pro emulating the boot flash.
	  The emulator watches the SPI bus for a command which is not a flash
	  access and passes what follows to the host, where it is shown by
	  'em100 --terminal'. This needs no wiring beyond the flash connection
	  which is already there, so it is useful on boards with no usable
	  UART.

config DEBUG_SANDBOX
	bool "Sandbox debug device"
	depends on SANDBOX
	default y if SANDBOX
	help
	  Provide a debug device for sandbox, which records what is written
	  to it so that tests can check it.

endif
